[# content/logo: the brand logo (or another logo you pass in), with the dark-mode swap.

   With no data it uses the brand logo from the tokens and, when the brand defines dark.logoUrl, swaps to it in
   dark mode. Pass src, alt (and optionally darkSrc) to show a different logo, for example a partner's.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: no dark-mode swap, so it always shows the light logo (the .logo-dark image stays hidden).
   - Gmail apps: may auto-invert colors and ignore prefers-color-scheme. Use a logo with a transparent
     background that reads on both light and dark if the swap matters.
   - Dark logo swap: only emitted when a dark logo exists (brand dark.logoUrl or darkSrc). #]
[% set src = data.src or t.logo.url %]
[% set alt = data.alt or t.logo.alt %]
[% set href = data.href or t.logo.href %]
[% set darkSrc = data.darkSrc or ((t.dark.logoUrl if t.dark else none) if not data.src else none) %]
<mj-image css-class="logo-light[[ ' ' + cls if cls else '' ]]" src="[[ src ]]" alt="[[ alt ]]" href="[[ href ]]" width="[[ s.width ]]" align="[[ s.align ]]" padding="[[ s.padding ]]" />
[% if darkSrc %]
<mj-image css-class="logo-dark[[ ' ' + cls if cls else '' ]]" src="[[ darkSrc ]]" alt="[[ alt ]]" href="[[ href ]]" width="[[ s.width ]]" align="[[ s.align ]]" padding="[[ s.padding ]]" />
[% endif %]
